1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,920
I am a fan of Ashito Aoi.

2
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:08,040
Probably his first in the world.

3
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,180
So there you have it.

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,000
No matter where you are, there could be fans listening in.

5
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,700
You should try and watch what you say.

6
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:18,400
Bye.

7
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:26,420
Oh, hey.

8
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:27,600
What's up?

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,560
You didn't hear that, did you?

10
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:44,480
Can I get that lunch?

11
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:48,300
You said that you had made an extra one.

12
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:49,500
Can I have it?

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,640
Uh.

14
00:02:24,018 --> 00:02:30,418
I've been wondering for a while now, how come you're always so gung-ho about helping me out?

15
00:02:31,438 --> 00:02:34,938
I said I was sorry. It's not like I was eavesdropping or anything.

16
00:02:35,458 --> 00:02:40,258
I took a seat on that bench, and then I heard the old man's voice followed by yours through the window.

17
00:02:41,238 --> 00:02:44,258
Someone said my name, and it's not like I could leave at that point.

18
00:02:44,818 --> 00:02:46,498
So I ended up hearing everything.

19
00:02:46,858 --> 00:02:49,398
You literally just described what eavesdropping is.

20
00:02:49,758 --> 00:02:51,838
Don't you have a match that you should be getting ready for?

21
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,618
Now please leave me alone.

22
00:02:54,318 --> 00:02:55,938
Right, in a sec.

23
00:02:57,238 --> 00:02:58,258
One more thing.

24
00:02:59,578 --> 00:03:03,318
I've been meaning to say thank you for persuading my mom and...

25
00:03:03,318 --> 00:03:04,178
Wait, Noriko?

26
00:03:05,398 --> 00:03:07,098
Oh yeah! That reminds me.

27
00:03:07,238 --> 00:03:10,138
I wanted to tell you the next time we met, your mom is amazing!

28
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,378
You really lucked out.

29
00:03:12,098 --> 00:03:13,298
Trust me on this one.

30
00:03:13,718 --> 00:03:16,718
Your mom and I ended up chatting about you a bunch over the phone.

31
00:03:16,958 --> 00:03:21,898
And from the way she went on about you, I could tell just how much she cared for you and wanted you to be happy.

32
00:03:21,898 --> 00:03:24,138
I know.

33
00:03:25,338 --> 00:03:26,798
You're a good person, Hana.

34
00:03:27,378 --> 00:03:27,638
Huh?

35
00:03:28,578 --> 00:03:30,698
That's what I was gonna say when we met again.

36
00:03:31,498 --> 00:03:32,718
You're a good person.

37
00:03:35,038 --> 00:03:35,778
I know.

38
00:03:35,778 --> 00:03:39,758
Of course you'd respond in such a cute way.

39
00:03:40,398 --> 00:03:42,938
Well, makes sense since you're cute.

40
00:03:43,698 --> 00:03:44,078
Uh...

41
00:03:44,078 --> 00:03:51,098
This whole soccer club thing ain't that bad.

42
00:03:51,298 --> 00:03:53,038
Certainly can't complain about the grub.

43
00:03:55,298 --> 00:03:56,418
Wait, hold on.

44
00:03:56,818 --> 00:03:58,318
What the heck did I even say?

45
00:03:58,438 --> 00:04:00,198
That didn't come out right, but you know what I meant.

46
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,818
So you wanted to know why I helped you?

47
00:04:04,338 --> 00:04:04,638
Huh?

48
00:04:05,638 --> 00:04:12,458
You see, the reason I keep on rooting for you is because you remind me of a certain player.

49
00:04:13,218 --> 00:04:16,518
That person is somebody very important to me.

50
00:04:17,658 --> 00:04:22,038
Whenever I watch you play, it brings me back to when I was his superfan.

51
00:04:22,598 --> 00:04:27,018
It's probably a bit selfish of me, since I'm doing it for my own sake.

52
00:04:27,018 --> 00:04:28,138
Oh.

53
00:04:29,158 --> 00:04:29,638
Really?

54
00:04:30,318 --> 00:04:32,158
I remind you of that guy, huh?

55
00:04:32,418 --> 00:04:35,198
In that case, he's gotta be an awesome player, right?

56
00:04:35,838 --> 00:04:36,058
Mm-hmm.

57
00:04:36,678 --> 00:04:36,938
Mm-hmm.

58
00:04:37,638 --> 00:04:38,598
So, hey, listen.

59
00:04:38,798 --> 00:04:40,478
I've got a little dream of my own.

60
00:04:40,798 --> 00:04:41,398
In the future...

61
00:04:42,858 --> 00:04:46,798
Wait just a second.

62
00:04:47,058 --> 00:04:48,078
Where is my lunch?

63
00:04:48,358 --> 00:04:50,058
Uh, I ate it all.

64
00:04:50,418 --> 00:04:51,198
It was good.

65
00:04:51,798 --> 00:04:53,718
Don't you have an important match soon?

66
00:04:53,858 --> 00:04:55,338
I said you could have one!

67
00:04:55,338 --> 00:04:57,418
Why would you stuff your face right before playing?

68
00:04:57,418 --> 00:04:58,418
I'm telling you it'll be fine!

69
00:04:58,518 --> 00:04:59,318
Stop worrying!

70
00:05:00,418 --> 00:05:01,798
Spin it out right now!

71
00:05:02,078 --> 00:05:03,578
Or else I'll have to take it back!

72
00:05:03,718 --> 00:05:04,838
Get your fingers out of my mouth!

73
00:05:06,918 --> 00:05:07,998
You crazy?

74
00:05:08,298 --> 00:05:09,518
I already ate it!

75
00:05:11,258 --> 00:05:14,438
If you want to go pro, you need to learn to take care of your body!

76
00:05:19,958 --> 00:05:21,338
What's up with that chick?

77
00:05:22,578 --> 00:05:23,418
She's scary.

78
00:05:23,418 --> 00:05:30,458
Today's match will be 7-on-7 between the new youth team players using half the field.

79
00:05:30,678 --> 00:05:34,638
It'll be a 30-minute best-of-one, and offsides rules will still apply.

80
00:05:34,898 --> 00:05:37,958
We don't have enough goalkeepers, so I'll be filling in for today.

81
00:05:38,638 --> 00:05:39,558
This will be fun.

82
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,518
What Fukuda mentioned earlier still stands.

83
00:05:43,118 --> 00:05:47,878
If during this match you show us your worth, you'll be promoted to the A-team immediately.

84
00:05:47,878 --> 00:05:53,078
Each team is instructed to follow a tactic that I come up with.

85
00:05:53,438 --> 00:05:57,658
And while you should stick to the general game plan, the minor details are up to you.

86
00:06:01,198 --> 00:06:03,038
There's no way he's going pro.

87
00:06:03,038 --> 00:06:19,298
I'm not going to let you write me off.

88
00:06:19,738 --> 00:06:23,578
Before I even get to play, I'll show you how wrong you are.

89
00:06:23,578 --> 00:06:29,078
I know you think I don't have a chance, you stone-faced jerk.

90
00:06:29,338 --> 00:06:32,698
But for me, going pro isn't a matter of if, but when.

91
00:06:33,258 --> 00:06:36,058
I won't stop until I'm a professional player.

92
00:06:36,298 --> 00:06:38,578
This isn't a matter of wanting or hoping for it.

93
00:06:38,758 --> 00:06:40,098
I know it's going to happen.

94
00:06:40,538 --> 00:06:45,258
That's why, even if my teammates or coaches don't believe in me, I couldn't care less.

95
00:06:45,258 --> 00:06:48,138
Besides, I already have tons of people rooting for me.

96
00:06:48,538 --> 00:06:51,298
I owe them so much, I can't let them down.

97
00:06:51,778 --> 00:06:54,118
This is my first step to becoming a pro.

98
00:06:55,638 --> 00:06:57,298
Right, here we go!

99
00:06:57,498 --> 00:07:01,038
Time to crush my first youth match and get my ticket straight to the A-team!

100
00:07:04,858 --> 00:07:05,338
Hit.

101
00:07:06,858 --> 00:07:07,378
Score.

102
00:07:07,858 --> 00:07:08,898
I've got a score.

103
00:07:09,378 --> 00:07:10,398
I'll show everybody!

104
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:12,298
Hey, Yuma!

105
00:07:13,498 --> 00:07:14,818
Pass the ball to me!

106
00:07:14,818 --> 00:07:17,578
I'll show you that I'm the reincarnation of Roberto Baccio!

107
00:07:17,858 --> 00:07:19,638
It doesn't matter that he's still alive!

108
00:07:20,978 --> 00:07:22,358
Man, you are wild!

109
00:07:22,598 --> 00:07:24,478
Give me the ball now!

110
00:07:25,338 --> 00:07:27,198
Over here! Pass it back to me!

111
00:07:27,498 --> 00:07:29,658
No, me! Give it to me!

112
00:07:31,558 --> 00:07:32,578
That's up, Corridor!

113
00:07:32,578 --> 00:07:50,198
Man, two inches lower and I would have made it!

114
00:07:50,278 --> 00:07:51,578
Wow, that was close!

115
00:07:51,578 --> 00:07:53,858
What are you doing, Togashi?

116
00:07:54,398 --> 00:07:59,078
Listen, I know you want to impress the coaches, but you shouldn't shove your own teammate to do it!

117
00:07:59,278 --> 00:08:03,378
I don't know if that's how you did things on your old team, but stop messing around!

118
00:08:03,378 --> 00:08:09,758
Hmm, you don't get it, dude. The only way to really show your stuff in a 30-minute half-field game like this is to score!

119
00:08:09,758 --> 00:08:13,258
Even the defenders need to try to make plays, you know?

120
00:08:13,258 --> 00:08:15,598
That's not a reason to be a jerk!

121
00:08:15,798 --> 00:08:17,958
You shouldn't steal the ball from your own team!

122
00:08:18,418 --> 00:08:19,498
Don't do it again!

123
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:22,798
Also, you're a defender, so act like one!

124
00:08:23,258 --> 00:08:25,898
Did you hear the sound the ball made when it bounced off the bar?

125
00:08:25,898 --> 00:08:30,778
Let's go!

126
00:08:31,318 --> 00:08:32,598
I'm gonna score!

127
00:08:33,238 --> 00:08:34,818
I have to score a goal!

128
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,738
He got that pass through to me?

129
00:08:40,498 --> 00:08:42,838
The ball came in at just the right angle and speed.

130
00:08:44,238 --> 00:08:45,878
This is no time to be impressed.

131
00:08:46,098 --> 00:08:49,038
If I want to score in a game at this level, I gotta stay focused.

132
00:08:55,898 --> 00:09:01,058
Aoi's just charging down the field? Will he pass it?

133
00:09:02,658 --> 00:09:04,598
Is he planning to do it alone?

134
00:09:05,978 --> 00:09:08,098
Hey! Don't try to dribble it through!

135
00:09:08,858 --> 00:09:11,578
Out to the wing! Let's attack down the wing!

136
00:09:12,538 --> 00:09:14,818
You're a defender, so act like one!

137
00:09:15,378 --> 00:09:18,598
I won't let you do anything that'll mess up my play, Togashi!

138
00:09:18,978 --> 00:09:21,298
You're a defender, just focus on your job!

139
00:09:21,758 --> 00:09:25,258
The coaches are watching! I'll score a goal and show them all!

140
00:09:25,258 --> 00:09:27,538
You better not get in my way!

141
00:09:32,118 --> 00:09:34,298
I don't care if it's egotistical.

142
00:09:34,878 --> 00:09:38,938
I know I'm being selfish, but I can't miss this chance.

143
00:09:39,758 --> 00:09:42,898
So in order to guarantee my spot on the A-team,

144
00:09:43,818 --> 00:09:46,878
I have to break through and score a goal!

145
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:58,118
Nice one!

146
00:09:59,498 --> 00:10:02,058
Oh, I guess he knows better than to charge right in.

147
00:10:02,918 --> 00:10:05,178
Masako, don't let number two get past you.

148
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,398
And keep your distance.

149
00:10:06,618 --> 00:10:07,538
Yeah, of course.

150
00:10:07,538 --> 00:10:09,818
We have enough people behind the ball.

151
00:10:10,298 --> 00:10:11,658
As long as we can hold the line.

152
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:18,478
Huh?

153
00:10:19,918 --> 00:10:20,898
What's he doing?

154
00:10:21,498 --> 00:10:22,618
He's just walking.

155
00:10:26,038 --> 00:10:27,578
Wait! Don't fall for it!

156
00:10:27,578 --> 00:10:28,638
Stay back!

157
00:10:28,638 --> 00:10:46,718
Eat that!

158
00:10:47,058 --> 00:10:48,758
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about!

159
00:10:48,838 --> 00:10:50,678
That was an amazing place, you dude!

160
00:10:50,678 --> 00:10:53,518
Wow, I can't believe Ashito actually scored a goal.

161
00:10:54,538 --> 00:10:56,858
But I still don't get what he just did.

162
00:10:58,538 --> 00:10:59,458
What was that?

163
00:10:59,978 --> 00:11:01,158
It doesn't make sense.

164
00:11:01,898 --> 00:11:04,018
Aoi was just aimlessly walking around.

165
00:11:05,078 --> 00:11:06,618
Then, all of a sudden,

166
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:08,278
he made a break for it.

167
00:11:08,678 --> 00:11:10,878
And he broke through the defensive line like it was nothing.

168
00:11:11,738 --> 00:11:12,318
But how?

169
00:11:12,618 --> 00:11:13,998
How in the world did that work?

170
00:11:14,758 --> 00:11:16,978
Mom, Shun, I did it!

171
00:11:17,258 --> 00:11:18,418
But I'm not done yet!

172
00:11:18,898 --> 00:11:20,978
You better get used to seeing more of that!

173
00:11:21,078 --> 00:11:25,138
Because I'm going to score another 3.86 trillion goals this game!

174
00:11:25,558 --> 00:11:27,058
Bravo, Ashito Aoi!

175
00:11:27,178 --> 00:11:28,298
Bravo, I say!

176
00:11:28,418 --> 00:11:30,078
You truly defy logic!

177
00:11:30,978 --> 00:11:32,798
The red team defended well.

178
00:11:32,898 --> 00:11:34,798
They cut off the other team's shooting opportunities

179
00:11:34,798 --> 00:11:36,158
and plugged all the gaps.

180
00:11:37,038 --> 00:11:39,698
But that changed when Aoi started to walk towards the goal.

181
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:42,078
It completely threw off their rhythm.

182
00:11:42,998 --> 00:11:46,638
No one would expect a player to start calmly walking forward in that situation.

183
00:11:47,338 --> 00:11:49,138
Their defense didn't know how to respond.

184
00:11:50,118 --> 00:11:53,018
That disruption drew Mosco out of his position in the defensive line,

185
00:11:53,478 --> 00:11:56,338
giving Aoi the chance to blow past him when he moved in too close.

186
00:11:56,638 --> 00:11:58,718
I still can't believe he actually pulled it off.

187
00:11:59,238 --> 00:12:01,478
A play like that is pretty much impossible to accomplish

188
00:12:01,478 --> 00:12:04,438
unless you know exactly how each player on the field is going to move.

189
00:12:06,538 --> 00:12:07,938
Hold on, Tsukishima.

190
00:12:08,218 --> 00:12:08,418
Hmm?

191
00:12:08,418 --> 00:12:11,418
That play, doesn't it feel a little off?

192
00:12:11,658 --> 00:12:12,838
I wouldn't celebrate yet.

193
00:12:13,138 --> 00:12:14,418
Dude, that was amazing!

194
00:12:15,238 --> 00:12:16,558
Ah-ha-ha-ha!

195
00:12:17,438 --> 00:12:20,118
That was a high-level play, especially from you.

196
00:12:20,718 --> 00:12:22,718
So, spill the beans, bro.

197
00:12:22,858 --> 00:12:23,998
When did you come up with it?

198
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:24,878
Oh.

199
00:12:25,698 --> 00:12:26,358
Oh, right.

200
00:12:26,498 --> 00:12:28,658
To be perfectly honest, I can't remember.

201
00:12:28,658 --> 00:12:34,278
Ashito Aoi, there's no question that he's got some interesting skills,

202
00:12:34,538 --> 00:12:37,238
but he has a critical flaw in his play style,

203
00:12:37,478 --> 00:12:39,378
which will prevent him from moving forward.

204
00:12:39,378 --> 00:12:54,178
You know, for a training game, it's getting pretty intense on the field.

205
00:12:54,178 --> 00:12:55,238
Watch out, Kurada.

206
00:12:55,598 --> 00:12:57,878
The parents over there are getting kind of restless.

207
00:12:58,758 --> 00:12:59,658
Can't blame them.

208
00:12:59,658 --> 00:13:03,738
See, I got scouted, and Ashito made it through the tryouts.

209
00:13:04,078 --> 00:13:07,298
But all you junior youth guys haven't made a single play so far.

210
00:13:07,878 --> 00:13:09,298
You guys gotta get moving.

211
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:12,738
Otherwise, Mommy and Daddy are gonna be so disappointed in you.

212
00:13:13,118 --> 00:13:17,198
Junior youth club players, you're a bunch of losers as far as I'm concerned.

213
00:13:17,198 --> 00:13:21,258
Masago, switch positions with me.

214
00:13:22,578 --> 00:13:25,938
If I don't put a stop to this now, he'll only annoy me more.

215
00:13:27,198 --> 00:13:28,058
Oh, yeah!

216
00:13:28,278 --> 00:13:29,978
Did you see that gold, you jerk?

217
00:13:30,178 --> 00:13:32,498
I bet you'll try to say that one isn't good enough.

218
00:13:32,798 --> 00:13:35,358
Then I'll have to keep scoring as many as I can!

219
00:13:42,358 --> 00:13:43,958
What amazing power, Togashi!

220
00:13:44,358 --> 00:13:47,098
Couple that with his burst of speed, and he's like a tank!

221
00:13:47,198 --> 00:13:48,578
You've gone far enough!

222
00:13:48,718 --> 00:13:50,018
Don't forget you're a defender!

223
00:13:50,458 --> 00:13:51,978
Pass me the ball and get back!

224
00:13:55,878 --> 00:13:56,858
Good job!

225
00:13:58,018 --> 00:13:58,258
Oh?

226
00:13:58,938 --> 00:13:59,458
Ah, sorry.

227
00:14:01,058 --> 00:14:05,058
Oh, you're asking for it!

228
00:14:07,398 --> 00:14:10,238
I became painfully aware during the tryouts

229
00:14:10,238 --> 00:14:12,498
that I was way behind the other youth players

230
00:14:12,498 --> 00:14:14,438
when it came to my ball handling skills.

231
00:14:14,438 --> 00:14:18,178
That's why, as soon as I got my acceptance letter,

232
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:20,598
I practiced day and night to get better.

233
00:14:20,898 --> 00:14:22,818
My old soccer club helped me train!

234
00:14:23,218 --> 00:14:24,498
I'll get past you!

235
00:14:24,498 --> 00:14:30,558
You idiot!

236
00:14:30,818 --> 00:14:32,118
What do you think you're doing?

237
00:14:33,718 --> 00:14:36,258
You're pushing your luck if you try to dribble it through!

238
00:14:36,598 --> 00:14:38,958
All you need to do is pass it to me like you did before!

239
00:14:39,218 --> 00:14:40,278
There's no rush here!

240
00:14:40,418 --> 00:14:41,838
We just have to move the ball around

241
00:14:41,838 --> 00:14:43,598
until we find an opening to attack from!

242
00:14:43,858 --> 00:14:45,138
It's how we play soccer!

243
00:14:45,678 --> 00:14:46,898
We gotta work together!

244
00:14:46,898 --> 00:14:47,858
We gotta work together!

245
00:14:47,858 --> 00:14:48,298
We gotta work together!

246
00:14:56,918 --> 00:14:57,018
Shit!

247
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,558
Ah!

248
00:14:59,558 --> 00:14:59,858
Owie!

249
00:15:00,218 --> 00:15:00,918
One more!

250
00:15:01,498 --> 00:15:03,818
I'll use my first touch trick!

251
00:15:04,498 --> 00:15:06,578
Then I'll land it right there!

252
00:15:06,858 --> 00:15:07,838
And pass him!

253
00:15:09,838 --> 00:15:11,038
I did it!

254
00:15:11,618 --> 00:15:12,118
Huh?

255
00:15:12,118 --> 00:15:23,278
what how did he predict that damn it ashito point your midsection in the direction you

256
00:15:23,278 --> 00:15:29,878
want to run i think i get it now let's go practice that trick on us until you've got

257
00:15:29,878 --> 00:15:35,538
it down pat we'll do whatever we can to help so you can crush it when you get to tokyo

258
00:15:35,538 --> 00:15:43,998
i'll break through i swear i'll break through oh man you said earlier that ashito has a critical

